// A process written with `main` in an image that names a console with no
// tick: it prints a line, which is posted and waits in the ring, since the
// driver runs only once this process parks, and ends with `sosmain.exit(5)`.
// The exit's `Sync` parks it until the driver has written the line, so the
// line comes before the kernel's exit line.

import sosmain

func main() {
    print("SOS consoleexit: a line, then sosmain.exit(5)")
    sosmain.exit(5)
}
